      "content": "PART A: CONCEPT OF PUBLIC FINANCE"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Public Finance examines how governments manage public expenditure, revenue generation, deficits, and public debt.",
        "Tax structures are classified into Progressive, Proportional, and Regressive based on tax rate variations relative to income levels.",
        "Fiscal Deficit indicates the total borrowing requirements of the government to cover total budgetary shortfalls.",
        "Primary Deficit isolates current year fiscal imbalance by subtracting past interest payment liabilities from the Fiscal Deficit.",
        "The Government Budget serves dual key objectives: optimal reallocation of resources and economic stabilization."
      ],
      "id": "c971ezq"
